1.40.m:
The Blessed One said:
"That true, imperishable Brahman is eighteenfold;
meditate upon that supreme abode which is the true immortal!"

1.41.m:
Brahmā said:
“His dwelling shall be in the mouth of the mare within the ocean;
water is my origin, O brāhmaṇa, and let him go to that immeasurable [realm].

1.42.m:
Vajrāṅga said:
"May no demonic disposition be mine; may imperishable worlds be mine;
may I take delight in austerity, and [may there be only] the maintenance of this body."

Vajrāṅga said:
"Arisen from deep contemplation at your command, I saw Varāṅgī;
terrified by Indra, she, desiring a son, said to me:
